  {
    "title": "The same event twice",
    "body": "The event queue delivers at least once, so \"order 123 shipped\" can reach two workers, or the same worker twice after a crash. Without a check, each delivery sends an email: the user gets **two**. Instead, each worker first inserts the **notification key** (event, user) into `sent`. The unique key accepts the first insert and rejects the second, so only one worker sends. Records are kept 7 days, longer than any redelivery: about 3 GB a day.",
