  {
    "title": "A crash after sending",
    "body": "A worker sends an email and crashes before recording \"sent\". After restart, it finds the key in status \"sending\" and cannot tell whether the provider got the email. **Send again**, and the user may get two; **don't**, and the user may get none. The email provider accepts an **idempotency key**: the retry uses the same notification key, and the provider drops the repeat. Push has no such key, so push errs on a rare miss; SMS login codes are sent before recording, so they err on a rare duplicate, because a missing code locks the user out.",
